  "note": "Borough election, 18 May 1949. Only the Town Hall Ward went to the poll, five candidates for four seats; the Market and Harryville Ward members were returned unopposed and are not itemised (Irish News, 20 May 1949, p. 3). Electorate 1,697; 960 voted; three spoiled papers. Mr. Murphy, a former Mayor and member for 29 years, was the only Catholic member and lost his seat."
